NOTICE — third-party components
===============================

Bark Desktop Client bundles or depends on the following third-party projects.
This file must be shipped with every binary distribution.

pypush 2.0.2 — https://github.com/beeper/pypush
  License: Server Side Public License v1 (SSPL-1.0)
  Used for: anonymous Apple device activation and the APNs courier client.
  IMPORTANT: the SSPL requires that anyone who offers the combined work as a
  service make the corresponding source available. This repository's own source
  is public; ship this dependency unmodified together with its license text.
  pypush is explicitly unstable until 3.0.0; the version is pinned and isolated
  behind bark_pc/push/pypush_client.py.

pystray 0.19.5 — https://github.com/moses-palmer/pystray
  License: GNU Lesser General Public License v3 (LGPL-3.0)
  Used for: the system tray icon and menu.

Pillow — https://python-pillow.org
  License: Historical Permission Notice and Disclaimer (HPND)
  Used for: thumbnails, tray/toast images, and the image viewer.

windows-toasts 1.3.1 — https://github.com/DatGuy1/Windows-Toasts
  License: MIT
  Used for: native Windows toast notifications, including hero images.

winrt-runtime / winrt-Windows.* — https://github.com/microsoft/pywinrt
  License: MIT
  Used by windows-toasts to reach the WinRT notification APIs.

segno — https://github.com/heuer/segno
  License: BSD 3-Clause
  Used for: QR code rendering in the setup wizard.

httpx — https://www.python-httpx.org
  License: BSD 3-Clause
  Used for: Bark server HTTP calls and image fetching.

anyio — https://anyio.readthedocs.io
  License: MIT
  Used for: the receiver's async task group and the pypush event loop.

websockets — https://github.com/python-websockets/websockets
  License: BSD 3-Clause
  Used for: the Supabase Realtime (`sb://`) WebSocket transport.

cryptography — https://cryptography.io
  License: Apache-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause
  Used for: loading the activation certificate/private key.

Python — https://www.python.org
  License: PSF License Agreement
  Bundled by PyInstaller in the portable build.

PyInstaller — https://pyinstaller.org
  License: GPL-2.0 with a special exception permitting distribution of bundled
  applications.
  Used only to produce the portable build.
